To achieve this, we need to add a **Web App Manifest**, a **Service Worker**, and ensure the HTML is mobile-first.

Here is the complete setup for your GitHub repository. You will need **three** files in your root directory.

### 1. `manifest.json`
This file tells the smartphone how the app should appear when installed on the home screen. Save this exactly as `manifest.json` in your repository.

```json
{
  "name": "Sandoug Savings",
  "short_name": "Sandoug",
  "description": "Savings account dashboard for members.",
  "start_url": "./index.html",
  "display": "standalone",
  "background_color": "#121212",
  "theme_color": "#121212",
  "icons": [
    {
      "src": "icon-192.png",
      "sizes": "192x192",
      "type": "image/png"
    },
    {
      "src": "icon-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png"
    }
  ]
}
